{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/45883-victorian-tales-of-decadence-and-death-jack-the-ripper","id":45883,"title":"Victorian Tales of Decadence and Death; Jack the Ripper","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-09T15:29:01-08:00","id":45883,"title":"Victorian Tales of Decadence and Death; Jack the Ripper","content":"Hallo everyone. I'm running a Geist: The Sin-Eaters game, set in the 1800th century London, and I want Jack The Ripper to be a part in that game. One of the themes I'm trying to run, in addition to the given themes that Geist has to it, is the indifference of the aristocracy, with regards to the suffering of the poor, and all the death it courses.<br /> <br /> My group consists of the following Sin-Eaters;<br /> Mr. Robert Luther; A brilliant, yet impoverished, Clocksmith, who was cheated out of his earnings by a greedy and uncaring employer, and subsequently died of disease in a moldy and cold shelter.<br /> Lady Elizabeth Wilde; The daughter of a rich family, the constant neglect of her parents and servants eventually lead to her leap off their family mansion. She walked away that day, and hasn't looked back since.<br /> Mr. Moses; Having been born to negro parents in the 1800's earned Moses a spot in a hellish slave pit, working, literally, untill the day he died. Having been proclaimed dead by his owners, he crawled out of the ditch they had thrown him into, and walked away as something of an oddity in the 1800's; a free negro.<br /> Mrs Lily Holton, a former prostitute whose brutal murder in an empty back alley and subsequent merging with her new passenger gave her all the resolve she needed to forge a better life for herself.<br /> <br /> As i said, I want to run with Jack The Ripper, and i was thinking of making him Lily Holtons murderer. While brainstorming, i came up with ideas such as a Blood Bather, who somehow needs the ectoplasm of ghosts to perform his/her bathing rite, a Slasher who have made a pact with a Kerberoi in exchange for/found a ritual that gives him immortality and a number of other things.<br /> <br /> My group tends to solve things with murder, which was one of my reasons for starting this Geist game. I dont like that. I dont want murder to be the easiest way out in this game. Therefor, it is important to my game, that the Ripper cannot be killed outright. That dosen't mean he has to be a one-man-army nor inherently immortal. I just need some gimmic for why the Sin-Eaters cant just slaughter him, even if they find out who he is (which i also plan to make insidiously difficult onto itself).<br /> <br /> I want him to be conning, cruel and uncaring for his fellow man, all the while upholding a mask of a charming, friendly and outgoing personality. Really key in that point i mentioned about, with the aristocracy being totally indifferent for the suffering of others, as long as it means they get ahead, and being damn proud of it. I also need it to be relevant to a Sin-Eater chronicle, after all, without it being too clich\u00e9d.<br /> <br /> I run my game very non-linear. Pretty much every session starts off by me asking &quot;Alright. You wake up your respective beds. What do you guys spend the day doing?&quot;.<br /> <br /> So. If you've endured my ramble, do you have any ideas for what i could do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T16:54:11-08:00","id":45912,"title":"","content":"A few comments:<br /> <br /> First, I find in &quot;My group does X, I want Y&quot; situations, correcting with game mechanics is not a good idea. Punishing them for what they want to do is really bad, but I won't go into detail there as it is not what you are discussing. Making them unable to solve it in a way they enjoy is less bad but still not great, as it is strongly prioritizing your fun over the groups. My recommendation is discuss what everyone wants and be sure everyone understands where everyone else is coming from, constructing a scenario as much as possible to take care of everyone's needs. This can include making an enemy not killable by pure violence, but it may be a little unfair to just drop that on them if it would make it less fun for them. So I strongly advise discussion over mechanics.<br /> <br /> To address your question directly, the simplest thing is have the being have some form of weakness like many Abmortals that is built into the requirement to kill him, possibly even hurt him. He does not need to be a one man army if the PCs cannot kill him. Of course, they can toss him into the underworld, seal him under cement, drop him in a furnace as an everlasting fuel source, or many other fates that won't kill him but make him effectively unable to funtion.<br /> <br /> The simplest way to deal with this is have a certain location (that they must find) that has a means that he can restore himself there if killed, or teleport himself there if needed. You could make the teleportation seriously limited in some way, given how WoD's power level works, say once a day or week, or even the new moon, something where dropping him in an oubliette will not solve it permenantly. Killing him may work too. If I might be so bold, tying it to something Egyptian may well work there; some of their funerary magic involved harvesting organs, Perhaps the person is a crazed Egyptologist, who found some artifact he can restore himself with (possibly even that once belonged to a tier 3 Krewe, or could be related to MTC) that must be destroyed to beat him.<br /> <br /> Biggest issues are twofold. 1) Immortals, and those who can rise from the dead, tend to look somewhat different to Sin-Eaters normal sight (they are not slowly dying, may have many types of deaths coming) so using any kind of immortal or dead riser is problematic IF they will deal with them in a different context. Players may well call bullshit if they looked totally normal to Sin-Eater sight. 2) Murder mysteries with Sin-Eaters is hard. They can interrigate ghosts and even with no ghosts can examine bodies to see what they saw or get information on their deaths. Be prepared for that. Having the killer never quite visible does not make a lot of sense unless he knows he is dealing with Necromancers, so you will want to be prepared for that. However, the Sin-Eaters sight won't necessarily go to visions, so you are well within your rights to have them see a face and not know about powers until they meet them. Know everything the PCs can do, especially in divination. At least as much as you foil, be sure you offer tidbits with their powers at least as much as you foil...preferably more.<br /> <br /> Other advice...if doing it sandboxy, be sure you have pleanty of stories, not this. I tried stocking my setting with tons of stories and it worked really well. Sandbox can be totally awesome, but it can be a &quot;Big Empty&quot; if the PCs are not finding your stories. Be prepared for that. I recommend discussing the PCs day to day activities before session 1 and have hooks ready to drop in those activities. That way they should find plenty of plots, and if the PCs ignore them that is not your fault. Second, the Victorian Era is a facinating time. I use the Castle Falkenstein sourcebook &quot;Comme Il Fault: All Things Right and Proper&quot; with all Victorian games, which is hard to get but this is a good oppertunity to immerse yourself in the politics, fashion, and technology of the era. I spent hours researching my Castle Falkenstein and victorian leg of my Vampire: The Masquerade game, and those were well spent hours.<br /> <br /> Happy to give more feedback as needed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T16:55:46-08:00","id":45914,"title":"","content":"First off, I feel ya. My Scion group is the same way. Kill them all and let the gods sort them out is their usual method unless I specifically dangle a different way in front of their faces.<br /> <br /> You could have The Ripper be a title and he an agent of a society. This society could have ties all over. This can make things difficult for the group. They can't just murder all of the agents. Instead, they have to take down the society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T22:37:07-08:00","id":46084,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/45883-victorian-tales-of-decadence-and-death-jack-the-ripper?p=45912#post45912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few comments:<br /> <br /> First, I find in &quot;My group does X, I want Y&quot; situations, correcting with game mechanics is not a good idea. Punishing them for what they want to do is really bad, but I won't go into detail there as it is not what you are discussing. Making them unable to solve it in a way they enjoy is less bad but still not great, as it is strongly prioritizing your fun over the groups. My recommendation is discuss what everyone wants and be sure everyone understands where everyone else is coming from, constructing a scenario as much as possible to take care of everyone's needs. This can include making an enemy not killable by pure violence, but it may be a little unfair to just drop that on them if it would make it less fun for them. So I strongly advise discussion over mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. You're right. I hadn't considered how my phrasing made me look.<br /> I don't think that killing is the only thing my group finds enjoyable. I think more a matter of &quot;If it isn't broken, don't fix it.&quot; and so far in our other games, killing has worked just fine <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I had thought about the Tier 3 Krewe thing, but then i just might have the can of wormsesque scenario, in which the Sin-Eaters steals the artifact, and have access to a host of Necromantic powers, that would make them too power too quickly.<br /> The thing about immortals looking different and ghostie-tattle-tales, is the reason i had thought about a Slasher who somehow needs ghost ectoplasm for whatever reason. That way, he'de look like an ordinary dude to Death Sight, and there would be no ghosts. Then they'd have to get to the bodies which are only police or family custody, which could be cool.<br /> Of course even if they did see a face, then London is a large city even at this time.<br /> <br /> I tend to just throw story hooks at them left and right, and have the group decide for themselves which ones they choose to pursue. I took heavy inspiration from a group from Book of the Dead, who worshipped Sin-Eaters, and threw that out there the same game session i introduced the killings, and now one of my players thinks they're tied into the killings.<br /> I find this style makes for more organic roleplay, in which the characters pursue storylines thematic to they're characters and their desires.<br /> <br /> You mention Egyptian lore, and i seem to remember Mummy being heavy on that. Is there any awesome stuff in that?<br /> <br /> <br /> To thedonnie;<br /> <br /> I dont think my players are quite powerful enough to take down an entire secret society of killers, but i like the idea. Do you think a longer story-arc about this society, would take too much focus away from the more central themes of Geist; The Sin-Eaters?<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks for both of your feedback guys. Much appreciated!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T02:43:40-08:00","id":46150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/45883-victorian-tales-of-decadence-and-death-jack-the-ripper?p=46084#post46084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. You're right. I hadn't considered how my phrasing made me look.<br /> I don't think that killing is the only thing my group finds enjoyable. I think more a matter of &quot;If it isn't broken, don't fix it.&quot; and so far in our other games, killing has worked just fine <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>All good, just mentioned in case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I had thought about the Tier 3 Krewe thing, but then i just might have the can of wormsesque scenario, in which the Sin-Eaters steals the artifact, and have access to a host of Necromantic powers, that would make them too power too quickly.<br /> The thing about immortals looking different and ghostie-tattle-tales, is the reason i had thought about a Slasher who somehow needs ghost ectoplasm for whatever reason. That way, he'de look like an ordinary dude to Death Sight, and there would be no ghosts. Then they'd have to get to the bodies which are only police or family custody, which could be cool.<br /> Of course even if they did see a face, then London is a large city even at this time. </div> </div> </div>This is true, but getting an artifact like that and knowing exactly how to use it are different. I am not saying it would be a useless hunk of ceramic (or whatever) to the Bound in question, but they may not know how to really use it unless they unlock its powers...future story point.<br /> <br /> I used a Slasher in an older story and essentially used a Mask as the power basis. Masks can be taken down by Sin-Eaters, but it takes more work. And yea, Slashers would look like ordinary dudes so that helps.<br /> <br /> If it were me, in their shoes, I would walk around that part of london using Deathsight to find people who will meet a violent end soon, and shadow them. You may want to be prepared for this plan. Which, I mean, could work, but might be a letdown if they try it session 1 (though people often overlook innate powers for dot ones, so you never know). If the Slasher can use Ectoplasm, though, he is no ordinary Slasher (which could be fine, but the more death touched the aura, the more obvious he should be to sin eater sight. Though your note on London being such a city is quite true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I tend to just throw story hooks at them left and right, and have the group decide for themselves which ones they choose to pursue. I took heavy inspiration from a group from Book of the Dead, who worshipped Sin-Eaters, and threw that out there the same game session i introduced the killings, and now one of my players thinks they're tied into the killings.<br /> I find this style makes for more organic roleplay, in which the characters pursue storylines thematic to they're characters and their desires. </div> </div> </div>I as well. It is very much the basis for my current Geist and Vampire games. I also found while it was a lot of work up front it is notably less ongoing work, which is nice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You mention Egyptian lore, and i seem to remember Mummy being heavy on that. Is there any awesome stuff in that? </div> </div> </div>Yes. A Mummy can be a very...interesting Antagonist. It would not be hard to try to build a reason for a Mummy Stalker, and trying to take one down in combat is difficult (though as always, A Krewe of Sin-Eaters verses a lone mummy would be rough on the Mummy). Mummies get weaker the longer they exist (till they die and start over) so it would make an odd form of antagonist.<br /> <br /> Mages also tend to be very difficult to kill. You could build a Mage's Arcana such that they are. I have a Necromantic Mage as a current antagonist in my Balance of Shadows game and he is kinda scary what he can do.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T03:15:46-08:00","id":46156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/45883-victorian-tales-of-decadence-and-death-jack-the-ripper?p=46150#post46150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is true, but getting an artifact like that and knowing exactly how to use it are different. I am not saying it would be a useless hunk of ceramic (or whatever) to the Bound in question, but they may not know how to really use it unless they unlock its powers...future story point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats actually a good point. They might need to find somebody who can help them, or venture to the Underworld for help and Necromantic know-how. Pretty good idea!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/45883-victorian-tales-of-decadence-and-death-jack-the-ripper?p=46150#post46150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I used a Slasher in an older story and essentially used a Mask as the power basis. Masks can be taken down by Sin-Eaters, but it takes more work. And yea, Slashers would look like ordinary dudes so that helps.<br /> <br /> If it were me, in their shoes, I would walk around that part of london using Deathsight to find people who will meet a violent end soon, and shadow them. You may want to be prepared for this plan. Which, I mean, could work, but might be a letdown if they try it session 1 (though people often overlook innate powers for dot ones, so you never know). If the Slasher can use Ectoplasm, though, he is no ordinary Slasher (which could be fine, but the more death touched the aura, the more obvious he should be to sin eater sight. Though your note on London being such a city is quite true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats actually pretty much what i want them to do. In my take of London, there are other things than Jack The Ripper preying on the poor citizendry. I'de abselutely adore it, if they took down a vampire or something, thinking themselves victorious over the grim murderer, only to realise that the vampire wasn't at all who they were really looking for. And then they'de have bloodsuckers to deal with aswell <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> A Mask would be too mindless and bloodlusty for what i have in mind. What do you think would work best as an intelligent and charming Slasher? A Charmer, a Psycho, a Maniac or a Genius?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/45883-victorian-tales-of-decadence-and-death-jack-the-ripper?p=46150#post46150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. A Mummy can be a very...interesting Antagonist. It would not be hard to try to build a reason for a Mummy Stalker, and trying to take one down in combat is difficult (though as always, A Krewe of Sin-Eaters verses a lone mummy would be rough on the Mummy). Mummies get weaker the longer they exist (till they die and start over) so it would make an odd form of antagonist.<br /> <br /> Mages also tend to be very difficult to kill. You could build a Mage's Arcana such that they are. I have a Necromantic Mage as a current antagonist in my Balance of Shadows game and he is kinda scary what he can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mummy thing sounds really interesting! I'de certain have to get my hands on that book. Its the only book (aside from the relatively new Demon) that i haven't read.<br /> Mages could be interesting too, but i think making a crazy murderer of a mage, would be alittle more flat than what i have planned for my mages. I'de like my mages to be genuinely nice people (to living anyway), but who view ghosts as little more than tools to be used, abused and thrown away. Would be much funnier if the Sin-Eaters are stuck between their liking of the Necromancers, but disgust at the way they treat the shades. And then we have the Geists who would probably be furious with such mages.<br /> Do you know if Death Sight can at all percieve mages, or if Sin-Eaters have any easy way to spot them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}